"""Original CPU PyTorch tensor, training and sequence-model contracts."""
from python_guide_core import t

t(18,'tensor-shape','Tensor dimensions are model contracts','A tensor shape records each axis length. Establish batch and feature meanings before choosing a layer, broadcast or loss; equal element counts do not imply interchangeable semantics.','Flattening erases the original axis contract.','a = torch.tensor(data)\nresult = list(a.shape)',[([[1,2],[3,4]],[2,2]),([[1,2,3]],[1,3])],'list(a.shape)','list(a.flatten().shape)')
t(18,'tensor-dtype','Choose floating tensors for fractional computation','An explicit floating dtype retains fractional inputs. Integer tensors cannot represent fractional model features and cannot require ordinary floating gradients.','Integer construction truncates fractional values.','result = torch.tensor(data,dtype=torch.float32).tolist()',[([1.5,2.5],[1.5,2.5]),([0.5],[0.5])],'dtype=torch.float32','dtype=torch.int64')
t(18,'tensor-broadcast','Broadcast tensor features deliberately','Tensor broadcasting aligns trailing axes. Verify both input shapes and the resulting shape; a valid broadcast can still express the wrong model operation.','A scalar offset is not a per-feature row vector.','matrix,row = data\nresult = (torch.tensor(matrix)+torch.tensor(row)).tolist()',[([[[1,2],[3,4]],[10,20]],[[11,22],[13,24]]),([[[0,0]],[1,2]],[[1,2]])],'torch.tensor(row)','torch.tensor(row)[0]')
t(18,'tensor-view','Tensor views can share storage','A slice normally shares tensor storage with its parent. clone creates an independent copy; detach changes gradient tracking while still sharing storage unless cloned.','Cloning the slice prevents mutation from updating the parent.','a = torch.tensor(data)\nb = a[1:]\nb.fill_(0)\nresult = a.tolist()',[([1,2,3],[1,0,0]),([5],[5])],'b = a[1:]','b = a[1:].clone()')
t(18,'scalar-gradient','Autograd accumulates derivatives on leaves','With requires_grad, PyTorch records differentiable operations and backward propagates derivatives. A leaf tensor receives its gradient; the computed value is not itself the gradient.','The derivative of x squared is twice x, not x.','x = torch.tensor(float(data),requires_grad=True)\ny = x*x\ny.backward()\nresult = float(x.grad)',[(3,6.0),(-2,-4.0)],'y = x*x','y = x')
t(18,'gradient-accumulation','Backward adds to existing gradients','Repeated backward calls add contributions to a leaf gradient. Clear gradients at the intended optimizer-step boundary; otherwise earlier batches remain in the accumulation.','Zeroing between contributions changes an intentional accumulated sum.','x = torch.tensor(float(data),requires_grad=True)\n(x*x).backward()\n(x*3).backward()\nresult = float(x.grad)',[(2,7.0),(0,3.0)],'(x*3).backward()','x.grad.zero_()\n(x*3).backward()')
t(18,'detach-boundary','Detach cuts the differentiation graph','detach returns a tensor without the prior autograd history. Use it for explicitly nondifferentiable boundaries; converting data to detach can unintentionally block intended learning.','Leaving the branch attached adds its derivative to the gradient.','x = torch.tensor(float(data),requires_grad=True)\ny = x*x + x.detach()*3\ny.backward()\nresult = float(x.grad)',[(2,4.0),(-1,-2.0)],'x.detach()*3','x*3')
t(18,'registered-parameters','Register trainable parameters on modules','nn.Parameter assigned as a module attribute is discovered by parameters and state_dict. A plain tensor attribute is not automatically an optimizable registered parameter.','An unregistered tensor is absent from the module parameter inventory.','class Model(torch.nn.Module):\n    def __init__(self):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.weight = torch.nn.Parameter(torch.tensor(float(data)))\nmodel = Model()\nresult = len(list(model.parameters()))',[(2,1),(0,1)],'torch.nn.Parameter(torch.tensor(float(data)))','torch.tensor(float(data))')
t(18,'logits-loss','Cross entropy expects logits','CrossEntropyLoss applies the stable log-softmax calculation internally. Supply raw class logits and integer target indices rather than applying softmax first.','Softmaxing twice changes the optimized loss.','logits = torch.tensor([data],dtype=torch.float32)\nresult = float(torch.nn.functional.cross_entropy(logits,torch.tensor([0])))',[([2.0,0.0],0.126928011),([0.0,0.0],0.6931471806)],'cross_entropy(logits,','cross_entropy(logits.softmax(dim=1),')
t(18,'optimizer-step','An optimizer applies a parameter update','After backward, an SGD step subtracts learning rate times the accumulated gradient. zero_grad controls the next accumulation cycle; step does not infer the loss by itself.','An ascent update moves the parameter in the opposite direction.','x = torch.nn.Parameter(torch.tensor(float(data)))\noptimizer = torch.optim.SGD([x],lr=0.1)\n(x*x).backward()\noptimizer.step()\nresult = float(x.detach())',[(2,1.6),(-1,-0.8)],'lr=0.1','lr=0.2')
t(18,'data-loader','DataLoader batches dataset records','A DataLoader combines dataset samples into batches. drop_last discards an incomplete final batch; keep it false when every record must contribute to this evaluation.','Discarding the final partial batch loses observations.','dataset = torch.utils.data.TensorDataset(torch.arange(data))\nloader = torch.utils.data.DataLoader(dataset,batch_size=2,drop_last=False,num_workers=0)\nresult = [batch[0].tolist() for batch in loader]',[(5,[[0,1],[2,3],[4]]),(2,[[0,1]])],'drop_last=False','drop_last=True')

t(19,'zero-grad-boundary','Reset gradients at the step boundary','zero_grad(set_to_none=True) removes previous gradient buffers. Accumulate intentionally within a step and reset before the next independent step.','Skipping the reset carries the previous derivative into the next step.','x = torch.nn.Parameter(torch.tensor(float(data)))\noptimizer = torch.optim.SGD([x],lr=0.1)\n(x*x).backward()\noptimizer.zero_grad(set_to_none=True)\n(x*3).backward()\nresult = float(x.grad)',[(2,3.0),(0,3.0)],'optimizer.zero_grad(set_to_none=True)','pass')
t(19,'eval-dropout','Evaluation mode changes module behavior','eval switches modules such as Dropout and BatchNorm to evaluation behavior. It does not disable gradient recording; use a separate grad-mode context for inference.','Leaving dropout in training mode changes this deterministic evaluation.','layer = torch.nn.Dropout(p=1.0)\nlayer.eval()\nresult = layer(torch.tensor(data,dtype=torch.float32)).tolist()',[([1,2],[1,2]),([0,3],[0,3])],'layer.eval()','layer.train()')
t(19,'no-grad-mode','Disable gradient recording explicitly','no_grad prevents recording operations performed inside its scope. It is separate from eval, which changes layer behavior but can still produce differentiable outputs.','An enabled grad context retains a graph when inference should not.','x = torch.tensor(float(data),requires_grad=True)\nwith torch.no_grad():\n    y = x*2\nresult = bool(y.requires_grad)',[(2,False),(0,False)],'torch.no_grad()','torch.enable_grad()')
t(19,'seed-scope','Seed the relevant random generators','manual_seed sets PyTorch random-generator state. Reproducibility also depends on data order, kernels, devices, package versions and other random libraries.','Drawing twice without reseeding advances the sequence.','torch.manual_seed(data)\na = torch.rand(4)\ntorch.manual_seed(data)\nb = torch.rand(4)\nresult = bool(torch.equal(a,b))',[(7,True),(42,True)],'torch.manual_seed(data)\nb','torch.manual_seed(data+1)\nb')
t(19,'checkpoint-weights','Restore model state explicitly','state_dict contains registered parameters and buffers. Save a state snapshot and load it into a compatible model; a Python object alias is not an immutable checkpoint.','An in-memory state dictionary without cloned values can track later mutations.','model = torch.nn.Linear(1,1,bias=False)\nwith torch.no_grad():\n    model.weight.fill_(data)\nstate = {k:v.clone() for k,v in model.state_dict().items()}\nwith torch.no_grad():\n    model.weight.add_(1)\nmodel.load_state_dict(state)\nresult = float(model.weight.detach().item())',[(2,2.0),(0,0.0)],'{k:v.clone() for k,v in model.state_dict().items()}','model.state_dict()')
t(19,'optimizer-resume','Resume optimizer state as well as weights','Stateful optimizers retain moments or momentum buffers beyond model parameters. A resumable checkpoint must include optimizer state and the training position.','A new optimizer without restored state has no momentum history.','x = torch.nn.Parameter(torch.tensor(float(data)))\noptimizer = torch.optim.SGD([x],lr=0.1,momentum=0.9)\n(x*x).backward()\noptimizer.step()\nstate = optimizer.state_dict()\nother = torch.optim.SGD([x],lr=0.1,momentum=0.9)\nother.load_state_dict(state)\nresult = len(other.state)',[(2,1),(1,1)],'other.load_state_dict(state)','pass')
t(19,'clip-gradients','Clip gradients before the update','clip_grad_norm_ rescales gradients whose combined norm exceeds a threshold. It modifies gradients, not parameter values, and must occur before optimizer.step.','Skipping clipping leaves this intentionally large gradient unchanged.','x = torch.nn.Parameter(torch.tensor(float(data)))\nx.grad = torch.tensor(10.0)\ntorch.nn.utils.clip_grad_norm_([x],max_norm=1.0)\nresult = float(x.grad)',[(2,1.0),(0,1.0)],'torch.nn.utils.clip_grad_norm_([x],max_norm=1.0)','pass')
t(19,'microbatch-scaling','Scale accumulated microbatch losses','To match the mean loss over equal-sized microbatches, divide each microbatch contribution by their count. Unequal batch sizes require weighting by observation count instead.','Adding unscaled batch losses multiplies the effective gradient.','x = torch.tensor(float(data),requires_grad=True)\nfor target in [1.0,3.0]:\n    ((x-target)**2/2).backward()\nresult = float(x.grad)',[(0,-4.0),(2,0.0)],'**2/2','**2')
t(19,'learning-rate-schedule','Track the schedule alongside optimizer state','A learning-rate scheduler changes optimizer settings over steps. Record its state and step timing when resuming; scheduler stepping is not itself a parameter update.','Omitting the scheduler step keeps the previous learning rate.','x = torch.nn.Parameter(torch.tensor(1.0))\noptimizer = torch.optim.SGD([x],lr=0.1)\nscheduler = torch.optim.lr_scheduler.StepLR(optimizer,step_size=1,gamma=0.5)\nfor _ in range(data):\n    optimizer.step()\n    scheduler.step()\nresult = optimizer.param_groups[0]["lr"]',[(1,0.05),(2,0.025)],'scheduler.step()','pass')
t(19,'tiny-overfit','Overfit a tiny batch as a diagnostic','A small deterministic training problem checks that gradients, loss and optimizer updates connect correctly. Falling training loss on this batch is a diagnostic, not evidence of generalization.','A zero learning rate prevents fitting this nonzero target.','torch.manual_seed(7)\nx = torch.tensor([[0.0],[1.0],[2.0]])\ny = 2*x+1\nmodel = torch.nn.Linear(1,1)\noptimizer = torch.optim.SGD(model.parameters(),lr=0.1)\nfor _ in range(200):\n    optimizer.zero_grad(set_to_none=True)\n    loss = ((model(x)-y)**2).mean()\n    loss.backward()\n    optimizer.step()\nresult = bool(((model(x)-y)**2).mean().item()<0.001)',[(1,True),(0,True)],'lr=0.1','lr=0.0')
t(19,'batchnorm-statistics','Batch normalization owns running statistics','BatchNorm updates running estimates during training and uses them in evaluation. Registered buffers must be checkpointed along with trainable parameters.','Evaluation mode does not update running training means.','layer = torch.nn.BatchNorm1d(1,momentum=1.0)\nlayer.train()\nlayer(torch.tensor(data,dtype=torch.float32).reshape(-1,1))\nresult = layer.running_mean.tolist()',[([2,4],[3.0]),([1,3],[2.0])],'layer.train()','layer.eval()')

t(20,'conv-output-shape','Convolution output depends on geometry','Convolution output length depends on input length, kernel size, stride, dilation and padding. Specify channels and spatial axes before constructing the layer.','Removing padding shrinks the spatial output.','x = torch.zeros(1,1,data,data)\nlayer = torch.nn.Conv2d(1,2,kernel_size=3,padding=1)\nresult = list(layer(x).shape)',[(4,[1,2,4,4]),(5,[1,2,5,5])],'padding=1','padding=0')
t(20,'spatial-pooling','Pooling reduces spatial resolution','Max pooling selects the largest value in each local window. It changes resolution and can lose spatial detail; average pooling encodes a different aggregation.','A mean is not the maximum of a pooling region.','x = torch.tensor(data,dtype=torch.float32).reshape(1,1,2,2)\nresult = torch.nn.functional.max_pool2d(x,2).flatten().tolist()',[([1,2,3,4],[4.0]),([-1,0,1,2],[2.0])],'max_pool2d','avg_pool2d')
t(20,'augmentation-consistency','Transform inputs and labels consistently','A horizontal image flip reverses the final spatial axis. Apply compatible transforms to spatial labels and restrict augmentation to the appropriate training scope.','Flipping the vertical axis creates a different spatial transform.','result = torch.tensor(data).flip(-1).tolist()',[([[1,2],[3,4]],[[2,1],[4,3]]),([[5,6]],[[6,5]])],'flip(-1)','flip(-2)')
t(20,'embedding-lookup','Embeddings index learned rows','An embedding maps integer token IDs to learned vectors. Padding indices and vocabulary boundaries are explicit data contracts, not arbitrary floating features.','Shifting token IDs changes which learned vectors are selected.','layer = torch.nn.Embedding(4,2)\nwith torch.no_grad():\n    layer.weight.copy_(torch.arange(8).reshape(4,2))\nresult = layer(torch.tensor(data)).tolist()',[([0,2],[[0,1],[4,5]]),([1],[[2,3]])],'layer(torch.tensor(data))','layer(torch.tensor(data)+1)')
t(20,'rnn-layout','RNN layouts distinguish batch and sequence','With batch_first=True, recurrent input is batch by sequence by feature. Hidden state still has layers by batch by hidden width, which is a separate layout.','Returning hidden-state shape in place of sequence-output shape changes the contract.','x = torch.zeros(2,data,3)\nlayer = torch.nn.RNN(3,4,batch_first=True)\noutput,hidden = layer(x)\nresult = list(output.shape)',[(5,[2,5,4]),(3,[2,3,4])],'list(output.shape)','list(hidden.shape)')
t(20,'lstm-state','LSTM carries hidden and cell state','An LSTM returns sequence outputs plus hidden and cell states. Preserve both states when carrying context; batch and layer dimensions must match the next invocation.','Flattening hidden and cell states loses their separate shapes.','layer = torch.nn.LSTM(3,4,batch_first=True)\noutput,(hidden,cell) = layer(torch.zeros(2,data,3))\nresult = [list(hidden.shape),list(cell.shape)]',[(5,[[1,2,4],[1,2,4]]),(2,[[1,2,4],[1,2,4]])],'list(cell.shape)','list(cell.flatten().shape)')
t(20,'causal-attention','Causal attention excludes future tokens','A causal attention mask restricts each position to its own and earlier keys. Without the mask, a token can read future information during autoregressive training.','Unmasked attention averages values from future positions in this example.','q = torch.ones(1,1,2,1)\nk = torch.ones(1,1,2,1)\nv = torch.tensor(data,dtype=torch.float32).reshape(1,1,2,1)\nresult = torch.nn.functional.scaled_dot_product_attention(q,k,v,is_causal=True).flatten().tolist()',[([2,4],[2,3]),([0,8],[0,4])],'is_causal=True','is_causal=False')
t(20,'attention-heads','Attention heads preserve a model-width contract','MultiheadAttention splits a model width across compatible heads and combines their results. Batch-first layout changes how the first two input axes are interpreted.','Flattening the attended output discards batch and token axes.','layer = torch.nn.MultiheadAttention(4,2,batch_first=True,dropout=0)\nx = torch.zeros(2,data,4)\noutput,_ = layer(x,x,x,need_weights=False)\nresult = list(output.shape)',[(3,[2,3,4]),(5,[2,5,4])],'list(output.shape)','list(output.flatten().shape)')
t(20,'padding-mask','Exclude padded tokens from loss','ignore_index excludes specified target entries from cross entropy. The mask belongs to target positions; confusing a real class with padding changes which examples train the model.','Treating the padding marker as a class is invalid.','logits = torch.zeros(2,2)\ntarget = torch.tensor([data,-100])\nresult = float(torch.nn.functional.cross_entropy(logits,target,ignore_index=-100))',[(0,0.6931471806),(1,0.6931471806)],'ignore_index=-100','ignore_index=-1')
t(20,'vocabulary-oov','Reserve an out-of-vocabulary token','A fixed vocabulary maps known tokens to stable IDs and unknown tokens to an explicit fallback. Fit vocabulary on training data rather than changing it during inference.','Using a real token ID for unknown text conflates distinct cases.','vocabulary = {"<unk>":0,"cat":1,"dog":2}\nresult = [vocabulary.get(word,0) for word in data]',[(['cat','bird'],[1,0]),(['dog'],[2])],'vocabulary.get(word,0)','vocabulary.get(word,1)')
t(20,'transformer-block','Transformer blocks retain token structure','TransformerEncoderLayer combines attention, normalization and a feed-forward sublayer while preserving model width. Its shape contract does not establish useful learned language behavior.','Returning a flattened tensor hides the token structure.','layer = torch.nn.TransformerEncoderLayer(d_model=4,nhead=2,dim_feedforward=8,batch_first=True,dropout=0)\nlayer.eval()\nwith torch.no_grad():\n    output = layer(torch.zeros(2,data,4))\nresult = list(output.shape)',[(3,[2,3,4]),(5,[2,5,4])],'list(output.shape)','list(output.flatten().shape)')
